// Title: Remote CHM File Download/Execution Via HH.EXE
// Sigma ID: f57c58b3-ee69-4ef5-9041-455bf39aaa89
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2022-09-29 | Modified: 2024-01-31
// ATT&CK: stealth, T1218.001
// Description: Detects the usage of "hh.exe" to execute/download remotely hosted ".chm" files.
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://www.splunk.com/en_us/blog/security/follina-for-protocol-handlers.html
//   - https://github.com/redcanaryco/atomic-red-team/blob/1cf4dd51f83dcb0ebe6ade902d6157ad2dbc6ac8/atomics/T1218.001/T1218.001.md
//   - https://www.zscaler.com/blogs/security-research/unintentional-leak-glimpse-attack-vectors-apt37
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_hh_chm_remote_download_or_execution.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, microsoft_xdr schema)

DeviceProcessEvents
| where (ProcessVersionInfoOriginalFileName =~ "HH.exe" or FolderPath endswith "\\hh.exe") and (ProcessCommandLine contains "http://" or ProcessCommandLine contains "https://" or ProcessCommandLine contains "\\\\")
